  'fr.namePlaceholder': 'Intrusion: door opened with no badge',
  'fr.nameHint': 'This is what an operator reads at 03:00 — name the conclusion, not the mechanism.',
  'fr.timingTitle': 'Timing',
  'fr.window': 'Window (seconds)',
  'fr.windowHint': 'How close in time the required events must be to count as one incident. It is the difference between “a door opened, and separately a camera saw motion last Tuesday” and a single event.',
  'fr.grace': 'Grace delay (seconds) — how long to wait before believing an absence',
  'fr.graceHint': 'When every required event has arrived, the rule does not fire — it ARMS, waits out this grace period, and only then decides whether the absence really held. A badge reader is routinely a second or two BEHIND the door contact it just authorised, so a swipe that lands inside the grace period DISARMS the rule: that was an authorised entry. Without this wait, the rule would cry intrusion on every legitimate badge entry, all day, until somebody turned it off.',
  'fr.graceDefaultHint': 'Left at 0, the rule waits 5 seconds.',
  'fr.cooldown': 'Cooldown (seconds)',
  'fr.cooldownHint': 'How long the rule stays quiet after firing, so one incident is one alert rather than a hundred. It survives a restart.',
  'fr.clauses': 'Conditions',
  'fr.clausesHint': 'A rule is a list of things that must have happened — and, crucially, things that must NOT have. The absences are what let a rule express innocence: without them, “the door opened at 03:00” is an alert every night a cleaner works late. A rule needs at least one thing that must happen — a rule made only of absences fires on nothing.',
  'fr.addRequired': 'Add something that must happen',
  'fr.addAbsent': 'Add something that must NOT have happened',
  'fr.noClauses': 'No conditions yet.',
  'fr.clauseN': 'Condition {n}',
  'fr.badgeRequired': 'Must happen',
  'fr.badgeAbsent': 'Must NOT have happened',
  'fr.absentNote': 'This is the half of the rule that expresses innocence. A matching event arriving within the grace delay DISARMS the rule instead of firing it — that is what stops a legitimate badge entry being reported as an intrusion.',
  'fr.mode': 'This event',
  'fr.modeRequired': 'must happen',
  'fr.modeAbsent': 'must NOT have happened',
  'fr.clauseKind': 'Node type',
  'fr.kindAny': 'Any node type',
