  'fr.clauseMatch': 'Text to match',
  'fr.matchPlaceholder': 'e.g. door opened',
  'fr.matchHint': 'Matched, case-insensitively, against the event’s title and body — in practice, the name of the rule that fired on the node (“Person detected”, “Front door opened”). A node’s own rule names are your vocabulary; you do not need to invent a taxonomy first.',
  'fr.fleetTitle': 'Nodes a rule can draw on',
  'fr.fleetHint': 'The control plane manages both kinds, and they are not interchangeable — motion belongs to a camera node; a door contact or a badge reader to a sensor node.',
